	(text "POWER  —  Power tree: VSYS input, regulators, AUX IN pass-through and monitoring  —  HW 0.1.0-proto.1" (at 40 20 0) (effects (font (size 4 4) (thickness 0.6)) (justify left)))
	(rectangle (start 30.48 41.91) (end 299.72 107.95) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "23b90c30-0c4f-b0b5-97fb-f7f2234bb172"))
	(text "VBUS pass switch to +5V" (at 33.02 45.72 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "A shortcut for plain 5 V USB. A regulator cannot make 5 V out of 5 V, so when the USB source is 5 V the board controller turns Q2 on and USB power goes straight onto the +5V rail. It\nis off by default and must stay off at 9 V, or 9 V would reach parts rated for 5.5 V; Q3 is the small transistor the controller uses to switch it." (at 33.02 50.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 30.48 128.27) (end 508.0 242.57) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "81192223-214d-a640-9a7c-52e6554e498e"))
	(text "input OR-ing" (at 33.02 132.08 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Where power enters. Two inputs feed one internal supply, VSYS: USB-C (5 V, or 9 V when a USB-PD charger agrees) and the J50 screw terminal (9-21 V). A diode on each (D3, D4) lets whichever is higher supply the board and stops one input from back-feeding the other. On the USB side, U26 is an electronic fuse: it ramps the voltage\nup gently so plugging in does not spark, cuts off above about 10 V or below 3.75 V, and limits current to about 2 A. D8 clamps voltage spikes on the screw input. VSYS then feeds the two main regulators." (at 33.02 137.16 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 30.48 262.89) (end 312.42 373.38) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "87d91be8-3614-a6f7-db7b-f1c92f2afa87"))
	(text "U11  VSYS to +5V" (at 33.02 266.7 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Switching regulator (buck converter) that makes +5V from VSYS. +5V feeds the 5 V buses, the extension 5 V pins and the four small regulators below. The board controller turns it on (EN_5V);\nthe pull-down keeps it off until then. The two feedback resistors set the output voltage; the inductor and capacitors are its power stage." (at 33.02 271.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 323.85 262.89) (end 638.81 373.38) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "b5d55e65-7943-b426-01fd-25f6d134bbd0"))
	(text "U12  VSYS to +3V3  (always-on AP63300 reference circuit)" (at 326.39 266.7 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Switching regulator that makes +3V3 from VSYS. It has no enable: it starts as soon as any power is present, because +3V3 runs the board controller, which then switches everything else on. Also powers the PSRAM, the\nflashes, the PHY and most logic. The two feedback resistors set 3.3 V; the inductor and capacitors are its power stage." (at 326.39 271.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 30.48 393.7) (end 279.4 514.35) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "6a18f406-4b40-d9c8-3127-e5630a70afea"))
	(text "U13  5V to +2V5" (at 33.02 397.51 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Small switching regulator that makes +2V5 from +5V for FPGA bank 16 (network) and the PHY's RGMII pins. Enabled by the board controller (EN_2V5); the feedback resistors\nset 2.5 V." (at 33.02 402.59 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 290.83 393.7) (end 539.75 514.35) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "101547a0-cfc0-5da4-e527-af55f21ccdb7"))
	(text "U14  5V to +1V8_IO" (at 293.37 397.51 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Small switching regulator that makes 1.8 V from +5V. Its output node is +1V8_IO: FPGA bank 13 and the 1.8 V memory on it, the 1.8 V position of the J19/J20 jumpers, and,\nthrough the bead below, the FPGA's auxiliary supply (VCCAUX) and its ADC as +1V8. Enabled by the board controller (EN_1V8); the feedback resistors set 1.8 V." (at 293.37 402.59 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 30.48 533.4) (end 279.4 654.05) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "f9f49d8f-2bbc-ab54-716f-8331bd806d9f"))
	(text "U16  5V to +1V2_MGT" (at 33.02 537.21 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Small switching regulator that makes +1V2_MGT from +5V for the FPGA transceivers' MGTAVTT supply. The transceivers are unused in rev A but must stay powered. Enabled by\nthe board controller (EN_1V2)." (at 33.02 542.29 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 290.83 533.4) (end 704.85 659.13) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "3230a9a4-976c-7fb7-38f1-b844c6e84944"))
	(text "U15  5V to +1V0  (4A FPGA core supply)" (at 293.37 537.21 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "The FPGA core supply: up to 4 A at 1.0 V from +5V, the heaviest rail on the board. Enabled by the board controller (EN_1V0); its power-good output (CORE_1V0_GOOD) is read through the status expander so firmware knows the core is up. The soft-start capacitor makes it ramp slowly; the\nfeedback resistors set 1.0 V." (at 293.37 542.29 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 30.48 679.45) (end 198.12 745.49) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "34b3a70f-8334-5377-f408-13de55b85b31"))
	(text "extension power protection control" (at 33.02 683.26 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Shared control for the four protected extension supplies (U21-U24). EXT_EN, from the board controller, turns\nthem all on; the pull-down keeps them off until firmware decides. EXT_FAULT is pulled up and goes low if any of\nthem (or the USB eFuse) detects a fault, so one controller pin hears all of them." (at 33.02 688.34 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 209.55 679.45) (end 378.46 792.48) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "c72c9fb2-6008-ac11-d91c-d1d956a148be"))
	(text "U21  +5V to +5V_EXT" (at 212.09 683.26 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Protected switch between the board's +5V and the 5 V pins of every extension port. Limits current to about 1 A\nand blocks current flowing back from an extension. Without it, a shorted extension would pull the whole board's\n5 V down." (at 212.09 688.34 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 389.89 679.45) (end 557.53 789.94) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "2e1a995d-1856-4644-d1f0-6a2a185310b1"))
	(text "U22  +3V3 to +3V3_EXT" (at 392.43 683.26 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Protected switch between +3V3 and the 3.3 V pins of every extension port, limited to about 0.5 A, with reverse\nblocking. Keeps a faulty extension from taking down the board controller's supply." (at 392.43 688.34 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 570.23 679.45) (end 737.87 789.94) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "5e5f7fcf-a1d4-2d9d-a61e-60cbb45b11b9"))
	(text "U23  VCCIO_1 to VCCIO_1_EXT" (at 572.77 683.26 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Protected switch for the PIN V supply of slots A-D (the voltage chosen on J19), limited to about 0.5 A, with\nreverse blocking." (at 572.77 688.34 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 30.48 812.8) (end 198.12 923.29) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "d1b93ab0-60db-d3c8-73de-5a7d49335efb"))
	(text "U24  VCCIO_2 to VCCIO_2_EXT" (at 33.02 816.61 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Protected switch for the PIN V supply of slots E-H (the voltage chosen on J20), limited to about 0.5 A, with\nreverse blocking." (at 33.02 821.69 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 209.55 812.8) (end 378.46 875.03) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "ab20ff13-141f-0690-d80c-c8493e9e26e7"))
	(text "MGTAVCC filter" (at 212.09 816.61 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "A small inductor and capacitor that make +1V0_MGT from +1V0: the same voltage, with the core's switching noise\nfiltered out, for the transceivers' MGTAVCC supply." (at 212.09 821.69 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 30.48 942.34) (end 510.54 1005.84) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "cf1a4f2d-b21a-6c00-ec91-376d02e46913"))
	(text "rail monitors" (at 33.02 946.15 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Lets the board controller measure every supply. Each rail goes to one of its analog inputs (ADC), which read 0-3.3 V. Rails at or below 3.3 V go through a 1 k resistor that protects the pin; VSYS and +5V are higher, so two resistors divide them down first. A 100 nF capacitor on each input steadies the reading. Firmware uses this\nto check each regulator came up before enabling the next." (at 33.02 951.23 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 521.97 942.34) (end 689.61 1003.3) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "dd6b19f4-23c2-07f7-e43e-2e021e9113f4"))
	(text "AUX IN" (at 524.51 946.15 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "Optional extra power for extensions that need more than 5 V (motors, LED strips, displays). Whatever you connect\nhere (9-28 V DC) goes, unregulated, to the AUX pin of every extension port through each port's own fuse. The\nboard itself never uses it." (at 524.51 951.23 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
	(rectangle (start 30.48 1026.16) (end 198.12 1097.28) (stroke (width 0.15) (type dash)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "18d682c0-eb87-a9a8-8330-8ea3edd58f41"))
	(text "VCCAUX filter" (at 33.02 1029.97 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (thickness 0.3)) (justify left)))
	(text "The split between +1V8_IO and +1V8. VCCAUX and VCCADC are the FPGA's internal supplies (clocking, I/O pre-\ndrivers, the XADC) and should not share copper with switching 1.8 V I/O loads, so they hang off U14's output\nthrough one ferrite bead (120 ohm at 100 MHz, 2 A, 50 mohm: 9 mV at the 0.18 A VCCAUX allowance, inside VCCAUX's\n1.71 V minimum). The 10 uF and 100 nF sit at U14's output beside its own capacitors; VCCAUX keeps its UG483\ndecoupling on the +1V8 side." (at 33.02 1035.05 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (italic yes)) (justify left top)))
